{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfcwFjez7vMzyYDjH17G1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the three candidate files, and the self-check passed. Its 100-draw smoke fit gave ELPD-LOO −3521.6, against −3531.2 for the incumbent's full fit. That comparison is only a hint, since the run was so short. The check also warned that PSIS-LOO looks unreliable: 7.5% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5, where the tolerance is 1%. Convergence, novelty against the other models and the full 30-minute fit were not tested here; admission tests those.\n\n**Name:** `default_side_guessing`\n\n**Hypothesis:** When a person guesses instead of comparing the two sequences, they don't pick a side at random. They press their usual default button. Each person has their own lean toward Left or Right, drawn from a population that may lean Left overall. When they do compare, they judge randomness exactly as the current best model does, with no side bias. So a side preference only shows up through guessing, and it is strongest in people who guess often.\n\n**Why this one:** The brief asked for a change to the decision rule, and the critique found two side-bias gaps. People's personal left-choice rates vary more than the model produces (p = 0.018), and the overall left-choice rate is slightly too high (p = 0.046). Neither survives the FDR correction (q = 0.14 and 0.18), so they are weak signals.\n\n**How it differs from what was tried:** `side_bias_streak_aversion_lapse` was pruned in experiment 2. It added a fixed push toward one button on every trial. Here the side preference applies only on guess trials, so it scales with each person's guessing rate and leaves decisive comparisons alone. One caveat: that earlier model didn't fit any better than the same model without the side push. That suggests a side term may not gain much here either.\n\n**Implementation:** It is the incumbent `most_lopsided_stretch_aversion` with one change. Guesses now press Left with a personal probability, set by a population model (`mu_side`, `sigma_side`, `z_side`, 400 participant slots), instead of choosing Left half the time.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_0/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2268,"cache_read_input_tokens":76240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2268,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b096d900-705f-4325-b5a2-ba4c83f8ed45","uuid":"08e8f9bc-7315-45c3-a67f-3c4c227ef6ea","timestamp":"2026-10-02T06:27:51.912Z","request_id":"req_011CfcwFj8UrDajKDkqFUB4s"}
